  bootwright / machine discover
      Boot inventory-only RHEL media on the selected powered-off physical machines, record
      authenticated Linux disk identities and power off. --name takes a comma-separated list.
      --dry-run previews without effects. --prepare-prerequisites also plans controller and
      infrastructure setup; review the complete plan before confirmation. Discovery never
      installs an OS or creates RAID volumes.

  Usage
    bootwright machine discover [flags]

  Command flags
      --dry-run                Preview the discovery plan without booting a machine
      --name                   Select comma-separated machine names (required)
      --prepare-prerequisites  Also plan and confirm controller and infrastructure
                               prerequisites
      --yes                    Confirm the command's ordinary confirmation

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright machine discover --context lab --name node --prepare-prerequisites --dry-run
